WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.005
Every open post starts with a decision. Who should be called next—and why?

2
00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:07.310
This is ReliefLedger.

3
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.009
Start with a clear view of the workspace.

4
00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:15.395
Here, three fictional officers and one open block give us a simple example

5
00:00:15.395 --> 00:00:16.070
to follow.

6
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.103
Open the roster to review the people behind the call list.

7
00:00:21.103 --> 00:00:25.870
Availability and overtime balances give the supervisor useful context before making a decision.

8
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:30.440
Next, select the open block and request an evaluation.

9
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:35.597
ReliefLedger returns an ordered recommendation from the service, using the rules configured for

10
00:00:35.597 --> 00:00:36.390
this demonstration.

11
00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.775
The result puts Jordan first, followed by Avery and Morgan.

12
00:00:40.775 --> 00:00:45.175
The reasons stay alongside the recommendation, so the supervisor can review the order

13
00:00:45.175 --> 00:00:46.190
rather than guess.

14
00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:53.274
The supervisor stays in control. This walkthrough uses fictional records and example rules;

15
00:00:53.274 --> 00:00:56.550
each facility’s policy is agreed before installation.

16
00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:04.590
ReliefLedger. Clarity for every overtime decision. Talk with us about your facility’s workflow.
